    "adapt": "The harbour wholesale warehouse (Garage_E_02, 28 x 19 m, one big ground-floor hall with truck bays all round, a mezzanine over the east end that stays). The kit shows the same model as the host, so its offsets are in the building's own frame, front +z. Both buying counters are plank workbenches (the buyers' cash boxes are wooden boxes). The buyer's counter stands mid-hall facing the front bays, the clerk behind it and the chalk price board beside it; the Coalman's Brow iron buyer has its own counter, clerk, platform scale and chalk board east of the wholesale counter (the mine has no till of its own); planks and logs stack along the west wall, ore bins and a barrel row along the back wall, cement and iron on pallets on the east side; work lights hang over the bays. Rows are rigid: shift, never stretch. Chandler counter (#4646): a third plank workbench west of the buyer counter, a coil of rope on it and a pile of fishing gear beside it; the ship chandler (Joseph Vidal, resident dock_chandler) takes the `counter` anchor behind it, bound to the dock wholesale place with m_sPlaceId (#4624)."
  },
